          "turn_index": 1,
          "type": "turn",
          "question": "Does that need treating?",
          "answer": "I'm not sure what \"that\" refers to. Which condition, symptom, or result do you mean? If you mean the cholesterol result from earlier, tell me the unit and the other values on that panel.\n\nIn general, the guidance I found suggests that treatment decisions depend on more than one number:\n\n- **Risk, not one value, often drives the decision.** For high blood pressure, drug treatment is tied to cardiovascular risk, not the blood pressure number alone. Lifestyle measures are the shared first step. (Hypertension guidance, major cardiology society consensus summary)\n- **Thresholds can be unclear.** For a mildly raised thyroid hormone level, there is broad agreement to treat when the level stays above about 10 mIU/L. Between the normal upper limit and 10, guidance differs, and some suggest monitoring alone for most people. (Hypothyroidism guidance, endocrinology summary)\n- **Impact on daily life matters.** For migraine, preventive treatment is usually offered when attacks are frequent or disabling. One common threshold is four or more migraine days a month with some disability. (Migraine guidance, national headache society summary)\n\nOnce you tell me the condition or finding, I can look for the guidance on that specific case. I can't tell you whether you personally need treatment. That decision needs a clinician who knows your full history.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
